[{:adr/id "2607122400"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-5820/6201 gain aggregate dashboard analytics; kotoba-lang/crm gains kotoba.crm.funnel"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-12"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/related ["2607121900-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-crm-coverage" "2607122100-cloud-itonami-isic-6201-marketing-coverage" "kotoba-lang/crm"]
  :adr/owner-directive "With Sales(5820)/Marketing(6201)/Service(6202, built independently in parallel) complete, owner directed deepening the three pillars with reporting/dashboard capability rather than adding new ISIC verticals. cloud-itonami-isic-6202 (built by a concurrent, independent session) was deliberately left untouched in this ADR's scope."
  :adr/new-technical-commons "kotoba-lang/crm gains a 4th module, kotoba.crm.funnel: stage-counts (point-in-time snapshot distribution, zero-filled), reached-counts (cumulative funnel view relying on kotoba.crm.pipeline's forward-only invariant), conversion-rate (nil on zero-denominator, never fabricated), coverage. Exit-stage entities are EXCLUDED from reached-counts/conversion-rate unless they carry an explicit :reached-stage fact -- never guessed. 21 tests/89 assertions, lint clean, commit a648f40c5c272e9bfba79f6b1407bb43f7402d16, pushed."
  :adr/isic-5820-dashboard "cloud-itonami-isic-5820 gains src/crm/dashboard.cljc: pipeline funnel + conversion rates via kotoba.crm.funnel over crm.facts/pipeline-stage-order, plus a ground-truth revenue rollup via kotoba.crm.revrec/recognized-revenue-to-date summed across every active subscription (never trusts a cached figure). New op :pipeline/dashboard-query, RBAC-restricted to :sales-manager only (a book-wide rollup is broader than any single account-holder's disclosure entitlement). Store protocol gained all-accounts (backward-compatible, contract-test parity proven). 37 tests/137 assertions, lint clean, commit 7f4ecb4699e9e1b709ebdf5fdd28d86bad45de8a, pushed."
  :adr/isic-6201-dashboard "cloud-itonami-isic-6201 gains src/marketing/dashboard.cljc, its FIRST aggregate-view capability (it deliberately has no per-record report.cljc): lead lifecycle funnel + conversion rates via kotoba.crm.funnel, campaign send/consent-rejection rollup (aggregating ledger facts the ConsentGovernor already produces, no new tracking invented), and a lead-score distribution always recomputed via kotoba.crm.leadscore/recompute-score (never the stored/cached score; stale contacts surfaced explicitly). New entitlement :marketing/view-dashboard added to policy/permissions, granted to :marketer/:marketing-manager. A real bug was found and fixed during this build: policy/hold-fact was dropping :campaign-id from rejected-send ledger facts entirely, which would have made per-campaign rejection rollup impossible -- fixed at the source in both hold-fact and operation.cljc's commit-fact, non-breaking. 38 tests/148 assertions, lint clean, commit 24fe2f61f7f76a5c12fb145da578fb9721ff4f52, pushed."
  :adr/scoped-exclusion "cloud-itonami-isic-6202 (customer-service hub) was NOT touched by this ADR -- it was built independently by a concurrent, unrelated session while this session was building 6201, and modifying someone else's just-shipped actor without coordination was deliberately avoided; a future dashboard addition to 6202 is left to its own owning session or a separate ADR"
  :adr/ground-truth-discipline-consistency "Both dashboards strictly extend this fleet's established 'never trust a cached/proposed figure, always recompute' discipline: 5820's revenue rollup reuses the exact same kotoba.crm.revrec recompute its own governor's revenue-mismatch-imminent gate already relies on; 6201's lead-score distribution reuses the exact same kotoba.crm.leadscore recompute its own governor's lead-score-mismatch gate already relies on. Neither dashboard invents a parallel, less-trustworthy shortcut."
  :adr/governance-pattern "Both new dashboard ops were gated by extending each actor's EXISTING RBAC permission table with a new entitlement, rather than defaulting to open access or inventing a parallel governance mechanism -- documented with explicit reasoning in each actor's own ADR-0001 addendum / DESIGN.md section"
  :adr/scope-note "This is a NEW ADR, not an addendum to ADR-2607121900/2607122100, because it spans a NEW cross-cutting technical-commons module (kotoba.crm.funnel) consumed by BOTH sibling actors simultaneously, rather than being scoped to either actor alone"}]
